    "comment": "What the developer's recordings (the private AdrianAbbas/Samples repository, MP3s in its root) contain, from its notes.txt, checked against the audio by prepare.py. Note names: C4 = MIDI 60. 'takes' is how many times each note was played (round-robins); 0 means it varies (counted from the audio). Synth sweeps ('kind': 'synth', Milestone 15b): one patch per WAV, every key of the Minilogue's 37 from lowest to highest; 'articulation' short or long (held: looped), 'patch' groups the two (one gain: same input gain per patch); pitches and octaves come from the audio (sweeps.py). Session 8: recordings may sit in subfolders and be WAV (found by file name anywhere below the source). The developer's notes name octaves with middle C = C3 (GarageBand's numbering): the voice's 'E2' sweeps start at 165 Hz (E3 here) and the 'G1' drones sound at 98 Hz (G2 here); every note is mapped at the pitch measured from the audio, the names below only order the notes. Kinds: 'hits' (takes per dynamic, soft to hard: velocity layers x round-robins), 'texture' (unpitched pieces the instrument picks from), 'chromatic' (an acoustic piano: every key, labelled by pitch evidence, the stretch tuning kept).",
